<%#
  THE QUESTION BEFORE A CHANGE — one dialog for the whole school app
  ==================================================================

  School's request (2026-09-16): “everywhere something is saved or deleted, ask once —
  do you really want to change this? — so that nothing goes wrong by mistake.”

  This partial is the dialog itself. `public/js/save-confirm.js` decides WHICH forms get
  asked and writes the words. A page never talks to this dialog directly: it either lets
  the shared asker handle its form, or says so in the form tag —

      data-confirm="own"    this form shows its own question (do not ask twice)
      data-confirm="off"    never ask about this form (a search, a download, a lookup)
      data-confirm-msg…     use my own words instead

  Included once per page from partials/footer.ejs (any signed-in user) and
  partials/public_footer.ejs (website forms).
%>
<div class="save-confirm-overlay" id="saveConfirm" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
     aria-labelledby="saveConfirmTitle" aria-describedby="saveConfirmMsg">
  <div class="save-confirm-box">
    <div class="save-confirm-icon" id="saveConfirmIcon" aria-hidden="true">💾</div>
    <h3 id="saveConfirmTitle">Apply the changes?</h3>
    <p id="saveConfirmMsg">Please check once before saying yes.</p>
    <p class="save-confirm-keys">Press <kbd>Esc</kbd> or “No, go back” to cancel — nothing is
      changed until you say yes.</p>
    <div class="save-confirm-actions">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline" id="saveNo">No, go back</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="saveYes">Yes, save</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
